       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1000 mg** twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg** three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose, but I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
